"Asserts a memory operation does not access bytes in host memory, or remote "
"connected peer device memory (the address must be device local). This is "
"intended for use with {ref}`atomicrmw <i_atomicrmw>` and other atomic "
"instructions. This is required to emit a native hardware instruction for "
"some {ref}`system scope <amdgpu-memory-scopes>` atomic operations on some "
"subtargets. For most integer atomic operations, this is a sufficient "
"restriction to emit a native atomic instruction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3209
msgid ""
"An {ref}`atomicrmw <i_atomicrmw>` without metadata will be treated "
"conservatively as required to preserve the operation behavior in all cases. "
"This will typically be used in conjunction with [!"
"amdgpu.no.fine.grained.memory](#amdgpu_no_fine_grained_memory)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3227
msgid "'`amdgpu.no.fine.grained.memory`' Metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3229
msgid ""
"Asserts a memory access does not access bytes allocated in fine-grained "
"allocated memory. This is intended for use with {ref}`atomicrmw "
"<i_atomicrmw>` and other atomic instructions. This is required to emit a "
"native hardware instruction for some {ref}`system scope <amdgpu-memory-"
"scopes>` atomic operations on some subtargets. An {ref}`atomicrmw "
"<i_atomicrmw>` without metadata will be treated conservatively as required "
"to preserve the operation behavior in all cases. This will typically be used "
"in conjunction with [!amdgpu.no.remote.memory.access]"
"(#amdgpu_no_remote_memory_access)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3252
msgid "'`atomic.ignore.denormal.mode`' Metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3254
msgid ""
"This is generic IR metadata for floating-point {ref}`atomicrmw "
"<i_atomicrmw>` operations; see {ref}`'atomic.ignore.denormal.mode' Metadata "
"<md_atomic.ignore.denormal.mode>` in the language reference for its "
"definition. It is required to emit a native atomic instruction for AMDGPU "
"global memory, which unconditionally flushes float denormals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3261
msgid ""
"On AMDGPU this is typically used in conjunction with [!"
"amdgpu.no.remote.memory.access](#amdgpu_no_remote_memory_access) and [!"
"amdgpu.no.fine.grained.memory](#amdgpu_no_fine_grained_memory)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3266
msgid "This metadata was previously named `amdgpu.ignore.denormal.mode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3277
msgid "'`amdgpu.expected.active.lanes`' Metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3279
msgid ""
"A profiling-derived hint describing how many lanes of the wavefront are "
"expected to be active. The metadata has a single `i32` constant operand "
"giving the expected number of active lanes as an absolute count (the same "
"value is used for both wave32 and wave64 targets). This structure is "
"enforced by the verifier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3285
msgid ""
"The AMDGPU atomic optimizer uses this metadata on LDS atomics to decide "
"whether to skip the DPP optimization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3296
msgid "'`amdgpu.cfs`' Metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3298
msgid ""
"Set the cache fill size (CFS) field in VMEM instructions for architectures "
"that support it. Can be used on memory instructions (e.g. load) and memory "
"intrinsics (e.g. llvm.amdgcn.image.load.1d)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3302
msgid "The default value for the CFS field is 0 (256 bytes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3304
msgid "Valid arguments for CFS Metadata are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3306
msgid "!{i32 1}  :  CFS_128B"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3307
msgid "!{i32 2}  :  CFS_64B"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3308
msgid "!{i32 3}  :  CFS_32B"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3310
msgid ""
"The field indicates how much data is fetched on a cache miss. It is only "
"supported on GFX13. GFX13 only honors it for load and atomic operations. "
"GFX13 does not support a 32-byte fetch size so it treats CFS_32B the same as "
"CFS_64B."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3316
msgid "'`amdgpu.noclobber`' Metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3318
msgid ""
"Consider the writes that a `load` instruction L marked as `!"
"amdgpu.noclobber` may see according to the {ref}`AMDGPU memory model<amdgpu-"
"location-order>`. L returns `undef` if any of these writes does not happen-"
"before the operation that dispatches the kernel executing L."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3323
msgid ""
"This metadata can allow the AMDGPU compiler backend to emit scalar instead "
"of vector load instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3326
msgid "LLVM IR Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3328
msgid "The AMDGPU backend supports the following LLVM IR attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3330
msgid "AMDGPU LLVM IR Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3335
msgid "LLVM Attribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3337
msgid "\"amdgpu-flat-work-group-size\"=\"min,max\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3338
msgid ""
"Specify the minimum and maximum flat work group sizes that will be specified "
"when the kernel is dispatched. Generated by the "
"`amdgpu_flat_work_group_size` CLANG attribute \\[{ref}`CLANG-ATTR <clang-"
"attr>`\\]. If the `reqd_work_group_size` metadata is present, the product of "
"its three workgroup size dimensions must match both `min` and `max`. The IR "
"implied default value is 1,1024. Clang may emit this attribute with more "
"restrictive bounds depending on language defaults. If the actual block or "
"workgroup size exceeds the limit at any point during the execution, the "
"behavior is undefined. For example, even if there is only one active thread "
"but the thread local id exceeds the limit, the behavior is undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3345
msgid "\"amdgpu-implicitarg-num-bytes\"=\"n\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3346
msgid ""
"Number of kernel argument bytes to add to the kernel argument block size for "
"the implicit arguments. This varies by OS and language (for OpenCL see {ref}"
"`opencl-kernel-implicit-arguments-appended-for-amdhsa-os-table`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3348
msgid "\"amdgpu-num-sgpr\"=\"n\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3349
msgid ""
"Deprecated. Specifies the number of SGPRs to use. Generated by the "
"`amdgpu_num_sgpr` CLANG attribute \\[{ref}`CLANG-ATTR <clang-attr>`\\]. Use "
"`\"amdgpu-waves-per-eu\"` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3353
msgid "\"amdgpu-num-vgpr\"=\"n\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3354
msgid ""
"Deprecated. Specifies the number of VGPRs to use. Generated by the "
"`amdgpu_num_vgpr` CLANG attribute \\[{ref}`CLANG-ATTR <clang-attr>`\\]. Use "
"`\"amdgpu-waves-per-eu\"` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3358
msgid "\"amdgpu-waves-per-eu\"=\"m,n\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3359
msgid ""
"Specify the minimum and maximum number of waves per execution unit. "
"Generated by the `amdgpu_waves_per_eu` CLANG attribute \\[{ref}`CLANG-ATTR "
"<clang-attr>`\\]. This is an optimization hint, and the backend may not be "
"able to satisfy the request. If the specified range is incompatible with the "
"function's \"amdgpu-flat-work-group-size\" value, the occupancy bounds "
"implied by the workgroup size take precedence. Under object linking, this "
"hint cannot lower occupancy below the ABI occupancy floor (and therefore "
"cannot raise the register cap); see {ref}`amdgpu-abi-occupancy`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3364
msgid "\"amdgpu-ieee\" true/false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3365
msgid ""
"GFX6-GFX11 (Except GFX11.7) Only Specify whether the function expects the "
"IEEE field of the mode register to be set on entry. Overrides the default "
"for the calling convention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3367
msgid "\"amdgpu-dx10-clamp\" true/false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3368
msgid ""
"GFX6-GFX11 (Except GFX11.7) Only Specify whether the function expects the "
"DX10_CLAMP field of the mode register to be set on entry. Overrides the "
"default for the calling convention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3370
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3371
msgid ""
"Indicates the function does not depend on the value of the "
"llvm.amdgcn.workitem.id.x intrinsic. If a function is marked with this "
"attribute, or reached through a call site marked with this attribute, and "
"that intrinsic is called, the behavior of the program is undefined. (Whole-"
"program undefined behavior is used here because, for example, the absence of "
"a required workitem ID in the preloaded register set can mean that all other "
"preloaded registers are earlier than the compilation assumed they would be.) "
"The backend can generally infer this during code generation, so typically "
"there is no benefit to frontends marking functions with this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3375
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-workitem-id-y\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3376
msgid ""
"The same as amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x, except for the "
"llvm.amdgcn.workitem.id.y intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3377
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-workitem-id-z\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3378
msgid ""
"The same as amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x, except for the "
"llvm.amdgcn.workitem.id.z intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3379
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-workgroup-id-x\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3380
msgid ""
"The same as amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x, except for the "
"llvm.amdgcn.workgroup.id.x intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3381
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-workgroup-id-y\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3382
msgid ""
"The same as amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x, except for the "
"llvm.amdgcn.workgroup.id.y intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3383
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-workgroup-id-z\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3384
msgid ""
"The same as amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x, except for the "
"llvm.amdgcn.workgroup.id.z intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3385
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-cluster-id-x\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3386
msgid ""
"The same as amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x, except for the llvm.amdgcn.cluster.id.x "
"intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3387
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-cluster-id-y\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3388
msgid ""
"The same as amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x, except for the llvm.amdgcn.cluster.id.y "
"intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3389
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-cluster-id-z\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3390
msgid ""
"The same as amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x, except for the llvm.amdgcn.cluster.id.z "
"intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3391
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-dispatch-ptr\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3392
msgid ""
"The same as amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x, except for the llvm.amdgcn.dispatch.ptr "
"intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3393
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-implicitarg-ptr\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3394
msgid ""
"The same as amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x, except for the "
"llvm.amdgcn.implicitarg.ptr intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3395
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-dispatch-id\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3396
msgid ""
"The same as amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x, except for the llvm.amdgcn.dispatch.id "
"intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3397
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-wwm\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3398
msgid ""
"The same as amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x, except for the llvm.amdgcn.strict.wwm "
"intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3399
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-queue-ptr\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3400
msgid ""
"Similar to amdgpu-no-workitem-id-x, except for the llvm.amdgcn.queue.ptr "
"intrinsic. Note that unlike the other ABI hint attributes, the queue pointer "
"may be required in situations where the intrinsic call does not directly "
"appear in the program. Some subtargets require the queue pointer to handle "
"some addrspacecasts, as well as the llvm.amdgcn.is.shared, "
"llvm.amdgcn.is.private, llvm.trap, and llvm.debug intrinsics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3403
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-hostcall-ptr\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3404
msgid ""
"Similar to amdgpu-no-implicitarg-ptr, except specific to the implicit kernel "
"argument that holds the pointer to the hostcall buffer. If this attribute is "
"absent, then the amdgpu-no-implicitarg-ptr is also removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3406
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-heap-ptr\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3407
msgid ""
"Similar to amdgpu-no-implicitarg-ptr, except specific to the implicit kernel "
"argument that holds the pointer to an initialized memory buffer that "
"conforms to the requirements of the malloc/free device library V1 version "
"implementation. If this attribute is absent, then the amdgpu-no-implicitarg-"
"ptr is also removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3409
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-multigrid-sync-arg\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3410
msgid ""
"Similar to amdgpu-no-implicitarg-ptr, except specific to the implicit kernel "
"argument that holds the multigrid synchronization pointer. If this attribute "
"is absent, then the amdgpu-no-implicitarg-ptr is also removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3412
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-default-queue\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3413
msgid ""
"Similar to amdgpu-no-implicitarg-ptr, except specific to the implicit kernel "
"argument that holds the default queue pointer. If this attribute is absent, "
"then the amdgpu-no-implicitarg-ptr is also removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3415
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-completion-action\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3416
msgid ""
"Similar to amdgpu-no-implicitarg-ptr, except specific to the implicit kernel "
"argument that holds the completion action pointer. If this attribute is "
"absent, then the amdgpu-no-implicitarg-ptr is also removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3418
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-lds-dma\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3419
msgid ""
"Indicates the function does not execute any {ref}`LDS DMA operations <amdgpu-"
"dma-operations>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3420
msgid "\"amdgpu-tg-split\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3421
msgid ""
"Enable threadgroup split execution mode for the function. This must be "
"consistently set (or unset) for all reachable functions. This is only "
"relevant on targets with the `tgsplit-support` feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3424
msgid "\"amdgpu-lds-size\"=\"min\\[,max\\]\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3425
msgid ""
"Min is the minimum number of bytes that will be allocated in the Local Data "
"Store at address zero. Variables are allocated within this frame using "
"absolute symbol metadata, primarily by the AMDGPULowerModuleLDS pass. "
"Optional max is the maximum number of bytes that will be allocated. Note "
"that min==max indicates that no further variables can be added to the frame. "
"This is an internal detail of how LDS variables are lowered, language front "
"ends should not set this attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3430
msgid "\"amdgpu-gds-size\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3431
msgid "Bytes expected to be allocated at the start of GDS memory at entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3432
msgid "\"amdgpu-git-ptr-high\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3433
msgid ""
"The hard-wired high half of the address of the global information table for "
"AMDPAL OS type. 0xffffffff represents no hard-wired high half, since current "
"hardware only allows a 16-bit value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3434
msgid "\"amdgpu-32bit-address-high-bits\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3435
msgid ""
"Assumed high 32-bits for 32-bit address spaces which are really truncated 64-"
"bit addresses (i.e., addrspace(6))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3436
msgid "\"amdgpu-color-export\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3437
msgid ""
"Indicates shader exports color information if set to 1. Defaults to 1 for "
"{ref}`amdgpu_ps <amdgpu-cc>`, and 0 for other calling conventions. "
"Determines the necessity and type of null exports when a shader terminates "
"early by killing lanes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3440
msgid "\"amdgpu-depth-export\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3441
msgid ""
"Indicates shader exports depth information if set to 1. Determines the "
"necessity and type of null exports when a shader terminates early by killing "
"lanes. A depth-only shader will export to depth channel when no null export "
"target is available (GFX11+)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3444
msgid "\"InitialPSInputAddr\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3445
msgid ""
"Set the initial value of the `spi_ps_input_addr` register for {ref}"
"`amdgpu_ps <amdgpu-cc>` shaders. Any bits enabled by this value will be "
"enabled in the final register value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3447
msgid "\"amdgpu-wave-priority-threshold\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3448
msgid ""
"VALU instruction count threshold for adjusting wave priority. If exceeded, "
"temporarily raise the wave priority at the start of the shader function "
"until its last VMEM instructions to allow younger waves to issue their VMEM "
"instructions as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3450
msgid "\"amdgpu-memory-bound\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3451 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3453
msgid "Set internally by backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3452
msgid "\"amdgpu-wave-limiter\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3454
msgid "\"amdgpu-unroll-threshold\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3455
msgid ""
"Set base cost threshold preference for loop unrolling within this function, "
"default is 300. Actual threshold may be varied by per-loop metadata or "
"reduced by heuristics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3457
msgid "\"amdgpu-partial-unroll-threshold\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3458
msgid ""
"Set base cost threshold preference for partial and runtime loop unrolling "
"within this function, default is 150. This is independent of `amdgpu-unroll-"
"threshold`, which controls the threshold used for full unrolling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3460
msgid "\"amdgpu-max-num-workgroups\"=\"x,y,z\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3461
msgid ""
"Specify the maximum number of work groups for the kernel dispatch in the X, "
"Y, and Z dimensions. Each number must be >= 1. Generated by the "
"`amdgpu_max_num_work_groups` CLANG attribute \\[{ref}`CLANG-ATTR <clang-"
"attr>`\\]. Clang only emits this attribute when all the three numbers are >= "
"1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3465
msgid "\"amdgpu-hidden-argument\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3466
msgid ""
"This attribute is used internally by the backend to mark function arguments "
"as hidden. Hidden arguments are managed by the compiler and are not part of "
"the explicit arguments supplied by the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3468
msgid "\"amdgpu-agpr-alloc\"=\"min(,max)\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3469
msgid ""
"Indicates a minimum and maximum range for the number of AGPRs to make "
"available to allocate. The values will be rounded up to the next multiple of "
"the allocation granularity (4). The minimum value is interpreted as the "
"minimum required number of AGPRs for the function to allocate (that is, the "
"function requires no more than min registers). If only one value is "
"specified, it is interpreted as the minimum register budget. The maximum "
"will restrict allocation to use no more than max AGPRs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3475
msgid ""
"The values may be ignored if satisfying it would violate other allocation "
"constraints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3477
msgid ""
"The behavior is undefined if a function which requires more AGPRs than the "
"lower bound is reached through any function marked with a higher value of "
"this attribute. A minimum value of 0 indicates the function does not require "
"any AGPRs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3480
msgid ""
"This is only relevant on targets with AGPRs which support accum_offset "
"(gfx90a+)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3481
msgid "\"amdgpu-sgpr-hazard-boundary-cull\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3482
msgid ""
"Enable insertion of SGPR hazard cull sequences at function call boundaries. "
"Cull sequence reduces future hazard waits, but has a performance cost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3484
msgid "\"amdgpu-sgpr-hazard-mem-wait-cull\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3485
msgid ""
"Enable insertion of SGPR hazard cull sequences before memory waits. Cull "
"sequence reduces future hazard waits, but has a performance cost. Attempt to "
"amortize cost by overlapping with memory accesses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3488
msgid "\"amdgpu-sgpr-hazard-mem-wait-cull-threshold\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3489
msgid ""
"Sets the number of active SGPR hazards that must be present before inserting "
"a cull sequence at a memory wait."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3490
msgid "\"amdgpu-promote-alloca-to-vector-max-regs\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3491
msgid "Maximum vector size (in 32b registers) to create when promoting alloca."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3492
msgid "\"amdgpu-promote-alloca-to-vector-vgpr-ratio\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3493
msgid "Ratio of VGPRs to budget for promoting alloca to vectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3494
msgid "\"amdgpu-dynamic-vgpr-block-size\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3495
msgid ""
"Represents the size of a VGPR block in the \"Dynamic VGPR\" hardware mode, "
"introduced in GFX12. A value of 0 (default) means that dynamic VGPRs are not "
"enabled. Valid values for GFX12+ are 16 and 32. Waves launched in this mode "
"may allocate or deallocate the VGPRs using dedicated instructions, but may "
"not send the DEALLOC_VGPRS message. If a shader has this attribute, then all "
"its callees must match its value. An amd_cs_chain CC function with this "
"enabled has an extra symbol prefixed with \"\\_dvgpr$\" with the value of "
"the function symbol, offset by one less than the number of dynamic VGPR "
"blocks required by the function encoded in bits 5..3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3501
msgid "\"amdgpu-cluster-dims\"=\"x,y,z\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3502
msgid ""
"Specify the cluster workgroup dimensions. A value of \"0,0,0\" indicates "
"that cluster is disabled. A value of \"1024,1024,1024\" indicates that "
"cluster is enabled, but the dimensions cannot be determined at compile time. "
"Any other value explicitly specifies the cluster dimensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3507
msgid "This is only relevant on targets with cluster support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3508
msgid "\"amdgpu-expert-scheduling-mode\" true/false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3509
msgid ""
"Enable expert scheduling mode 2 for this function. This is a hardware "
"execution mode introduced in GFX12."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3512
msgid "This is only relevant on GFX12+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3513
msgid "\"amdgpu-expand-waitcnt-profiling\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3514
msgid ""
"Enable expansion of s_waitcnt instructions for profiling purposes. When "
"enabled, each s_waitcnt instruction that waits on multiple counter types is "
"expanded into a sequence of s_waitcnt instructions, each waiting on a single "
"counter type. This allows PC-sampling based profilers to attribute wait "
"cycles to specific counter types (e.g., VMEM, LDS, EXP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3517
msgid "\"amdgpu-no-fwd-progress\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3518
msgid "Disable forward progress mode for wave priority (enabled by default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3520
msgid "Relevant for GFX10+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3523
msgid "Calling Conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3525
msgid "The AMDGPU backend supports the following calling conventions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3527
msgid "AMDGPU Calling Conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3532
msgid "Calling Convention"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3534
msgid "`ccc`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3535
msgid ""
"The C calling convention. Used by default. See {ref}`amdgpu-amdhsa-function-"
"call-convention-non-kernel-functions` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3538
msgid "`fastcc`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3539
msgid "The fast calling convention. Mostly the same as the `ccc`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3541
msgid "`coldcc`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3542
msgid "The cold calling convention. Mostly the same as the `ccc`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3544
msgid "`amdgpu_cs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3545
msgid "Used for Mesa/AMDPAL compute shaders. ..TODO:: Describe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3546
msgid "`amdgpu_cs_chain`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3547
msgid "Similar to `amdgpu_cs`, with differences described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3549
msgid ""
"Functions with this calling convention cannot be called directly. They must "
"instead be launched via the `llvm.amdgcn.cs.chain` intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3552
msgid ""
"Arguments are passed in SGPRs, starting at s0, if they have the `inreg` "
"attribute, and in VGPRs otherwise, starting at v8. Using more SGPRs or VGPRs "
"than available in the subtarget is not allowed. On subtargets that use a "
"scratch buffer descriptor (as opposed to `scratch_{load,store}_*` "
"instructions), the scratch buffer descriptor is passed in s\\[48:51\\]. This "
"limits the SGPR / `inreg` arguments to the equivalent of 48 dwords; using "
"more than that is not allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3557
msgid ""
"The return type must be void. Varargs, sret, byval, byref, inalloca, "
"preallocated are not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3560
msgid ""
"Values in scalar registers as well as v0-v7 are not preserved. Values in "
"VGPRs starting at v8 are not preserved for the active lanes, but must be "
"saved by the callee for inactive lanes when using WWM (a notable exception "
"is when the llvm.amdgcn.init.whole.wave intrinsic is used in the function - "
"in this case the backend assumes that there are no inactive lanes upon "
"entry; any inactive lanes that need to be preserved must be explicitly "
"present in the IR)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3563
msgid ""
"Chain functions receive a stack pointer from their caller (in s32), similar "
"to `amdgpu_gfx` functions. This points to the bottom of the stack. "
"Referencing values on the caller's stack is undefined behaviour. If needed, "
"the frame pointer is s33 and the base pointer is s34. Calls to `amdgpu_gfx` "
"functions are allowed and behave like they do in `amdgpu_cs` functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3568
msgid ""
"A function may have multiple exits (e.g. one chain exit and one plain `ret "
"void` for when the wave ends), but all `llvm.amdgcn.cs.chain` exits must be "
"in uniform control flow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3569
msgid "`amdgpu_cs_chain_preserve`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3570
msgid ""
"Same as `amdgpu_cs_chain`, but active lanes for VGPRs starting at v8 are "
"preserved. Calls to `amdgpu_gfx` functions are not allowed, and any calls to "
"`llvm.amdgcn.cs.chain` must not pass more VGPR arguments than the caller's "
"VGPR function parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3572
msgid "`amdgpu_es`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3573
msgid ""
"Used for AMDPAL shader stage before geometry shader if geometry is in use. "
"So either the domain (= tessellation evaluation) shader if tessellation is "
"in use, or otherwise the vertex shader. ..TODO:: Describe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3575
msgid "`amdgpu_gfx`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3576
msgid ""
"Used for AMD graphics targets. Functions with this calling convention cannot "
"be used as entry points. ..TODO:: Describe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3578
msgid "`amdgpu_gfx_whole_wave`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3579
msgid ""
"Used for AMD graphics targets. Functions with this calling convention cannot "
"be used as entry points. They must have an i1 as the first argument, which "
"will be mapped to the value of EXEC on entry into the function. Other "
"arguments will contain poison in their inactive lanes. Similarly, the return "
"value for the inactive lanes is poison."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3585
msgid ""
"The function will run with all lanes enabled, i.e. EXEC will be set to -1 in "
"the prologue and restored to its original value in the epilogue. The "
"inactive lanes will be preserved for all the registers used by the function. "
"Active lanes only will only be preserved for the callee saved registers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3589
msgid ""
"In all other respects, functions with this calling convention behave like "
"`amdgpu_gfx` functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3590
msgid "`amdgpu_gs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3591
msgid "Used for Mesa/AMDPAL geometry shaders. ..TODO:: Describe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3592
msgid "`amdgpu_hs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3593
msgid ""
"Used for Mesa/AMDPAL hull shaders (= tessellation control shaders). ..TODO:: "
"Describe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3594
msgid "`amdgpu_kernel`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3595
msgid "See {ref}`amdgpu-amdhsa-function-call-convention-kernel-functions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3596
msgid "`amdgpu_ls`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3597
msgid ""
"Used for AMDPAL vertex shader if tessellation is in use. ..TODO:: Describe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3598
msgid "`amdgpu_ps`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3599
msgid "Used for Mesa/AMDPAL pixel shaders. ..TODO:: Describe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3600
msgid "`amdgpu_vs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3601
msgid ""
"Used for Mesa/AMDPAL last shader stage before rasterization (vertex shader "
"if tessellation and geometry are not in use, or otherwise copy shader if one "
"is needed). ..TODO:: Describe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3604
msgid ""
"The following ABI conventions apply to all calling conventions that are used "
"for callable functions (i.e. those that do not correspond to hardware entry "
"points):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3607
msgid ""
"On entry to a function the dependency counters (`VMcnt`, `LOADcnt` etc.) are "
"in an indeterminate state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3609
msgid ""
"On return from a function, all dependency counters must be zero except for "
"`VScnt`/`STOREcnt` or `VMcnt`/`LOADcnt` if the only outstanding operations "
"are `global_inv` or `buffer_inv`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3613
msgid ""
"For entry points, the ABI conventions are dictated by the hardware behavior "
"at wave launch and wave termination:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3616
msgid ""
"When a wave is launched the shader can assume that all dependency counters "
"are zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3618
msgid ""
"The shader can leave the dependency counters in any state before terminating "
"the wave (e.g. with `s_endpgm`)."
msgstr ""

